      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:194:4",
      "text": [
        " إِذَا زَارَ الْحَاجُّ مِنْ مِنًى فَخَرَجَ مِنْ مَكَّةَ فَجَاوَزَ بُيُوتَ مَكَّةَ فَنَامَ ثُمَّ أَصْبَحَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ مِنًى فَلَا شَيْ‏ءَ عَلَيْهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hisham Bin Al Hakam, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘When the pilgrim visits (the Kabah) from Mina, so he goes out from Makkah, and exceeds the houses of Makkah, so he sleeps, then it is morning before he comes to Mina, then there is nothing upon him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hisham ibn al-Hakam who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If one performing al-Hajj visits the House from Mina’, then comes out of Makkah and sleeps, and it becomes dawn before reaching Mina’, he is not obligated for anything in this matter.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
